File System Management
-	ls – list  #show list of contents
-	touch <file-name> - will create empty files
-	touch <f1, f2, f3, f4> - will create multiple files at once
-	mkdir <folder-name> - will create a empty folder
-	mkdir <f1, f2, f3> - will create multiple folders
-	rm – removes files
-	rmdir – removes empty folders 
-	rm -rf -   deletes files and folders 
-	echo – will read input to output 
-	cat <file-name> - will read contnt from file
-	cat > file-name – we can add content to the file with cat
-	cat f1 f2 f3 > f4 – we can combine content from multiple files into 1 

Copying and Moving Files

- cp file /path - will create a duplicate file in new loc
- cp file file1 - will create a duplicate file with new name
- mv file /path - will move the original to the new loc
- mv file new-file - changes name of the file







